  "details": "<p>The <em>tribus Maecia</em>, according to Livy, was established for new citizens. According to Festus,\u00a0the tribe took its name from an encampment of the Volscians near Lanuvium.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Tribus Maecia (originally Maicia) was a later rural tribe of ancient Rome, established in 332 B.C.",
